menu "gogo"

    config GOGO_KBD
        bool "Keyboard port (kbd)"
        default y
        help
            Build the TCA8418 keyboard driver and the I2C bus it needs
            (Cardputer ADV; no effect on the StickS3, which has no keyboard).
            When off, port.Open("kbd") returns ok=false and the IDF I2C
            master driver is not linked into the Cardputer firmware.

    config GOGO_BATTERY
        bool "Battery port (power)"
        default y
        help
            Build the battery reader: the ADC divider on the Cardputer, the
            M5PM1 on the StickS3. When off, port.Open("power") returns
            ok=false. The StickS3 still uses I2C for the PM1 LCD rail when
            the console is on.

    config GOGO_NET
        bool "Network (Wi-Fi + net stack)"
        default y
        help
            Build the Wi-Fi station driver and gogo's net stack (netif, udp,
            tcp, tcp_listen ports). When off, the capability "net" is absent
            (an image that needs it is refused at boot), port.Open of those
            ports returns ok=false, net.Subscribe returns false, and
            `gogo config scan` answers "no network in this firmware" and `stats`
            prints only the memory figures.
            esp_wifi, wpa_supplicant, libnet80211, libpp and libphy are not linked.

    config GOGO_SD
        bool "microSD card (/sd on FatFs)"
        default y
        help
            Build fs_fat.c (the /sd backend on FatFs) and the SD driver
            (Cardputer ADV; no effect on the StickS3, which has no slot).
            When off, /sd is not registered (every path is NotMounted),
            CAP_SD is absent, and FatFs, sdmmc and sdspi are not linked.
            The SD pins (G12, G14, G39, G40) stay reserved: the card slot
            is still wired to them, so the gpio port keeps refusing them.

    config GOGO_FS_EXFAT
        bool "exFAT on the SD card"
        depends on GOGO_SD
        default y
        help
            Compile FatFs with exFAT (FF_FS_EXFAT 1, components/fatfs/src
            /ffconf.h). When off, only FAT12/16/32 mount; an exFAT card
            fails with the existing "no FAT or exFAT file system" message
            and /sd stays NotMounted.

    config GOGO_IMU
        bool "Motion sensor port (imu)"
        default y
        help
            Build the BMI270 IMU driver (imu_esp.c, both boards, on the
            shared I2C bus) and its 8 KB legacy configuration (Bosch,
            BSD-3). When off, CAP_IMU is absent (an image that needs it is
            refused at boot), port.Open("imu") returns ok=false, and on the
            Cardputer with GOGO_KBD also off the IDF I2C driver is not
            linked.

    config GOGO_IR
        bool "Infrared ports (ir_tx, ir_rx)"
        default y
        help
            Build the RMT infrared drivers (ir_esp.c): ir_tx on both
            boards (StickS3 G46, Cardputer G44), ir_rx on the StickS3 only
            (G42). When off, CAP_IR_TX and CAP_IR_RX are absent, port.Open
            of those ports returns ok=false, and the IDF RMT driver is not
            linked.

    config GOGO_AUDIO
        bool "Audio ports (mic, spk)"
        default y
        select I2S_ISR_IRAM_SAFE
        help
            Build the audio drivers (audio_esp.c): mic and spk on both
            boards (ES8311 codec and I2S), and make the I2S interrupt
            IRAM-safe so a /flash write does not lose or replay DMA
            buffers. When off, CAP_MIC and CAP_SPK are absent, port.Open
            of those ports returns ok=false, and the IDF I2S driver is not
            linked.

    config GOGO_FONT_CJK
        bool "Chinese console font (GB 2312)"
        default y
        help
            Embed gogo12.font (printable ASCII plus GB 2312, 162958 bytes).
            When off, embed gogo12-ascii.font (printable ASCII only, 1536
            bytes) and every other character shows as the console's box.

endmenu
